          "path": "_m/g/c/q/g/battlefield-line-railway-wp/the-battlefield-line-market-bo.jpg",
          "filename": "The Battlefield Line, Market Bosworth - geograph.org.uk - 590450.jpg",
          "caption": "The Battlefield Line, Market Bosworth The Battlefield Line is the name given to this short stretch of heritage railway between Shenton and Shackerstone; trains run mainly on summer weekends, and a few other days out of season. The line was originally part of a route between Nuneaton and Ashby de la Zouch; regular passenger services were withdrawn by the LMS as early as 1931 although it continued to be used for coal trains until 1971.",
          "alt": "The Battlefield Line, Market Bosworth The Battlefield Line is the name given to this short stretch of heritage railway between Shenton and Shackerstone; trains run mainly on summer weekends, and a few other days out of season. The line was originally part of a route between Nuneaton and Ashby de la Zouch; regular passenger services were withdrawn by the LMS as early as 1931 although it continued to be used for coal trains until 1971.",
